<description>&lt;p&gt;Stephen Miller is confronting his first crisis as White House chief of staff while the United States deploys drones to strike ELN guerrilla elements operating inside Venezuela, adding external military pressure. Venezuela has pledged to finish repairs on the Colombia pipeline by March and more than half of its population faces near-daily blackouts, prompting some thirty-somethings in finance and tech to begin returning. JD Vance and his oil donor deny a secret meeting before a raid on Venezuela, and a legal strategy is being pursued to free Nicolás Maduro. Aldo Torres notes each barrel of oil extracted leaves a Venezuelan household in the dark, a Panamanian journalist’s home was set ablaze and a Venezuelan intelligence chief’s lawyer was found dead in a Madrid storage room. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxQVUJGTmU0OUlnNHg1QVdVRUZsQVZkMWZ2MzhqRFBIMzFxOUNpN3AtUUl6a1lSZnNnZ3hpbUJUeFNqLS1mNlJtVHJtRk1UZFhNNmU1X0ZkS083UEF1S3F1TUJHS0tOaF9PalpmVEJMZjg2blpsRHVHeU05enVwakI2cFc0LXhmM3loeWotMkNyVGxsZEh5VVhxeDNZQzJtdnRlMGZaMGxiYXp3V0JnZWFwT2ZzYw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxOanFOSUk5RG52VjUxZm5QcWhXb0lSUHRHWlhGUlVvQk9qSkl4eXVxV0tIX1I0U0U2d1RMNGJoNFFzcncxTmFpNU5NZnIzdlB0cTR5cTFLejhxM2FXZTdicDVHZmI0amlIZG5nMnFLTkxYZzM5aDFQWjVHaS1sSlAtUDhwLU43OGhYNFdjSkZIRTh2X1lMc2JabWxnWF9vSk93a1ZyZ2VwLXFXd3oxSzByT3Nn?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxPNngtTTdNNWh2YXdsTUNwRVo3NHZIY3JqcU1zaVBZdGdiODBGMmtaNTRDN1JWbmlpNERtc1l2UzB3VGdwZnlJQktOWTFJdl9qX3RxUW5vWl9RWFJjRE5ZTzNhQnM1eTFUaEdTV2JwODF1dlRVRVBPSkkzdmhDdE0yUV93b1ZPdWpNazhxbFBWY0FEdmt6VUh0Ri1iQzc1YnNMOVA2TnIyYUhIaG1VeDdGejBaVQ